1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:03,650
You want to type with your eyes on the page.

2
00:00:03,600 --> 00:00:05,010
Good.

3
00:00:05,010 --> 00:00:07,589
We start with the hands.

4
00:00:07,589 --> 00:00:09,877
Find F and J.

5
00:00:09,877 --> 00:00:13,135
Those two keys have a small bump.

6
00:00:13,135 --> 00:00:15,395
That bump is home.

7
00:00:15,395 --> 00:00:17,470
Close your eyes.

8
00:00:17,470 --> 00:00:20,050
Index fingers only.

9
00:00:20,050 --> 00:00:22,230
Find the bumps.

10
00:00:22,230 --> 00:00:24,065
Don't peek.

11
00:00:24,065 --> 00:00:29,930
Left index stays on F. Right index stays on J. That is the home row.

12
00:00:29,930 --> 00:00:35,355
Curve the other fingers onto A S D and K L semicolon.

13
00:00:35,355 --> 00:00:37,909
Thumbs rest on space.

14
00:00:37,909 --> 00:00:44,252
To type U, the right index steps up one key, then walks straight back to J.

15
00:00:44,252 --> 00:00:46,034
One rule.

16
00:00:46,034 --> 00:00:49,518
Never look down at the keys while you type.

17
00:00:49,518 --> 00:00:52,004
The bumps bring you home.

18
00:00:52,004 --> 00:00:54,690
The screen holds your eyes.

19
00:00:54,690 --> 00:00:59,651
After a few days the hands move and the mind stays on the words.

20
00:00:59,651 --> 00:01:01,233
Ready.

21
00:01:01,233 --> 00:01:03,932
First drill is the home row.

22
00:01:03,932 --> 00:01:05,675
Let's go.

